You are running HEADLESS. Never wait for input and never end your turn to wait for a notification: poll in loops instead. Hard time box: 90 minutes. Commit and push to main after each milestone.

First run `entire session current` and stop if no session is shown or the id is f5117257-5211-42ae-823c-32aa228a28d9.

You are B8a. Read ~/brief/FRONTEND-BRIEF-v2.md fully (the spec) and site/web/PROGRESS.md (v1's state). v2 replaces the site's whole visual layer: dark, cinematic, image-rich, animated. Keep the data layer, tests and QA scripts.

In parallel, session B8-3D builds `src/three/HeroScene.tsx` and `public/hero-poster*` on branch `site-3d` (it will be merged later). **Do NOT create files under `src/three/` or named `hero-poster*`.** Build the hero with a `HeroVisual.tsx` slot that shows your best photo for now. The 3D and its poster get wired in after the merge.

Milestones:
1. (≤10 min) **Vercel.** The owner is logging the box into Vercel (device flow in tmux session `vlogin`). Check `vercel whoami` between the other milestones, without blocking; continue with milestones 2–3 meanwhile.
   Once logged in:
   - in site/web, `vercel link --yes --project heirloom`;
   - add `vercel.json` (framework vite, outputDirectory dist, a 404 fallback);
   - make the Vite `base` come from `VITE_BASE` (default `/`).
2. (≤20 min) **Design system** per the brief:
   - dark tokens, fonts (Instrument Serif, Geist, Geist Mono via fontsource; subset);
   - hallmark SVG (an "H" in a guilloché ring) + favicon;
   - `scripts/guilloche.mjs` (rosettes and wave bands as SVG);
   - Lenis smooth scroll (off under reduced motion);
   - motion helpers: word-reveal headline, count-up, magnetic button, in-view reveal, spotlight hover.
3. (≤15 min) **Photography.**
   - Find 4–6 Unsplash photos (WebSearch/WebFetch on unsplash.com): macro watch movement, engraved metal or guilloché dial, brass gears, archive drawers or library. Check that each is under the Unsplash License.
   - Download via `https://unsplash.com/photos/<id>/download?force=true`, grade them dark with a brass feel and compress with sharp to responsive AVIF and WebP (each ≤180 kB).
   - Record id, photographer and URL in `site/web/ASSETS.md`.
4. (≤40 min) **Beats 1–6 of the brief:**
   - hero (word-reveal headline "Old software, *kept honest.*", sub, three count-up figures from data, magnetic CTAs, HeroVisual);
   - the full-bleed photo section with parallax and engraved version plates;
   - **"Watch it work"**, the pinned scroll-driven campaign (3D-tilted 19x3 tile register on a bezel dial, data-driven captions, tiles stamping in, the 87890→15307 connector drawing at Oct 6, the query pulse on 15307, live counters; a vertical story on mobile);
   - the finding (date plates locking around "5 days", terminal typing FAIL x3, the verbatim claim);
   - the register restyled as an engraved certificate (spotlight hover);
   - the receipt as a certificate (tilt, guilloché frame, the calibration triangle as an animated instrument diagram).
   Remove or hide v1 sections not yet restyled: B8b does beats 7–12.
5. (≤10 min) Build and deploy to Vercel production:
   - `vercel pull --yes --environment=production`, then `vercel build --prod`, then `vercel deploy --prebuilt --prod`;
   - try `vercel alias set <deployment-url> heirloom-proof.vercel.app` (else another free clean name);
   - curl until 200;
   - record the URL in PROGRESS.md and print it.
6. (≤10 min) Quick QA: run the QA script (update selectors as needed), Read the 1440 and 390 PNGs, fix the worst issues, redeploy.

Rules:
- Every number from site.json.
- Copy plain and honest ("candidate backports"; the exact Ubuntu claim sentence; no exploitability claim).
- Never print .env values.
- Run `python3 ~/brief/secretscan.py` before the final push.

Finish with:
- the Vercel URL and its status;
- `git log -5 --format='%h %s | %(trailers:key=Entire-Checkpoint,valueonly)'`;
- what B8b should do next (also in PROGRESS.md).

